    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:2e780f63f4172747",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "b8ac46f7c420705a541e562c3992b96fe4647643868d2cf268170c38381010ab",
      "text": "Follow the trails and viewpoints of Iguaçu National Park through the Atlantic Forest. Giant ferns, vines and araucarias grow here. Coatis often appear near the trails. The forest is also home to toucans, macaws, capuchins and rarer animals such as jaguars.\n\nThe Brazilian side gives you a wide view of the whole waterfall system. Water pours down in several lines, with the most powerful section, the Devil’s Throat, plunging into a deep gorge. The falls are about 72–80 metres high. From here you can see the contrast between the calm flow above the ledge and the churning water below.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw62hpb8-lj4ic-amanda",
        "model": "ChatGPT",
        "wordAbsenceReason": "The Word excursion gives a different account of the watercourse and omits this block’s forest species, height range and contrast above and below the ledge."
      }
    },
